On the topic of buying wishs vs. stealing them:  
Just because a shopkeeper sells wishs doesn't mean 
that there is any "physical" manifestation of the
wish to steal.  That is, the shop keeper may have 
a nontransferable ability to grant wishs.  If you kill 
them, or otherwise piss them off, you will not have 
access to the wishs.  Sort of like at a temple...if
you kill the priest/ess you may not gain so much, but
the ability to make donations can be very useful.

Personally, while I like the idea of being able to 
buy some common stuff at a shop that need not actually
be sitting in view, I feel that buying wishs is
unnecessary.  This is because you can already get 
them from other places, say fountains or thrones, 
albeit with some risk.  Other things like potions
of healing or water, or most certainly scrolls of
identify would be helpful.  As an alternative to
scrolls of identify, perhaps the shopkeeper could
have an innate ability (cf. above) to identify things
for a price.  Thus it might be worthwhile not to
rob every shop you come across so you can have access
to identifies.  Or you can just read the spoilers
and learn how to identify most stuff without scrolls.

I, for one, would like features that limit the amount 
of dicking around at the keyboard necessary to do 
stupid simple tasks.  For instance, to be able to 
mark a location and then have a command to go to that
location by the quickest known route (1 key stroke).  
This is not a teleport as it will take "actual time"
to get there and it could abort if you run into 
unfriendly monsters.  It should allow you to go
up/down stairs as well, as long as you have been
there before.  Typically, there is an altar, say two
levels up, and I have a corpse to deal with but just
don't feel like dealing with it.  Or perhaps a weapon
stash or something....

